<!--
    Search glyph, used by Explore's search field and its search button.

    Converted from the Figma header icon (118:578). Path data is verbatim
    from the export; the geometry is not redrawn.

    SIZING: the export is a 16x16.0023 leaf; the group maps its 16-unit frame onto
    19.7 units of this 24 viewport — the ink height of ic_notification_bell,
    which is staying and is therefore the fixed reference every other header
    icon is matched to. That also lands within 1.5% of the design's own 20dp
    spec. scale 1.23125 with translate (2.15, 2.1486) centres it.

    fillType is deliberately absent: the export carries no fill-rule, so it
    uses non-zero, which is Android's default too. Forcing evenOdd would
    invert the knockouts.

    Closest of the four to what it replaces (IoU 0.83) — same glyph, but the old
    one was about 16% lighter in ink. Replaced so it does not read thinner than
    the four exact glyphs beside it.

    The 16x16.0023 source is very slightly non-square; uniform scale preserves
    that, so the height lands at 19.7028 rather than exactly 19.7.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <group
        android:scaleX="1.23125"
        android:scaleY="1.23125"
        android:translateX="2.15"
        android:translateY="2.1486">
        <path
